Please read our updated purchasing terms below before you ship. They apply
to every order our company places with you from this week onward, and they
replace the terms we sent at the start of the season. Our order for this
week is at the very end of this message, after the terms, so please read all
the way down.

Delivery. Goods are to be delivered to the receiving dock named on the
order, between the hours our receiving team keeps open on working days.
Deliveries that arrive outside those hours may be turned away, and the cost
of a second attempt falls on the carrier you choose. If a delivery will be
late, tell our buyer as soon as you know, by email, with the new expected
date and the reason. A delivery that arrives in part is accepted in part;
the rest stays on order unless our buyer cancels it in writing.

Packing. Each carton must carry a packing slip that names our order number,
the items inside and how many of each. Cartons must be sealed, labelled on
two sides and stacked so that the heaviest are at the bottom of the pallet.
Fragile goods must be marked as fragile on every side. Pallets must be
wrapped, must not overhang their base and must be safe for a forklift to
lift. Loose items in a shared carton must be bagged and labelled by item so
that our receiving team can count them without opening every bag.

Substitutions. Do not substitute any item for another without our buyer's
written agreement, even when you believe the substitute to be equal or
better. If an item is no longer made, or cannot be supplied in time, tell
our buyer before you ship and wait for an answer. Goods sent as unagreed
substitutes may be returned at your cost, and the original item stays on
order until our buyer cancels it or you supply it.

Prices. The price on our order is the price we pay. A change of price must
be agreed in writing by our buyer before the goods are shipped; an invoice
at a higher price than the order will be held until the difference is
resolved. Prices include packing and labelling as described above. Freight
is paid as agreed for your account, and where nothing has been agreed,
freight is paid by you and is not added to the invoice.

Invoices. Send one invoice for each delivery, to our accounts address,
quoting our order number and the delivery note it belongs to. An invoice
that does not quote an order number cannot be matched and will be returned
to you unpaid. Credit notes must quote the invoice they correct. We pay
correct invoices at the end of the month that follows the month of delivery,
by bank transfer, to the account you have given us in writing.

Quality. Goods must match the description on the order and any drawing or
sample our buyer has agreed with you. Goods that are damaged, faulty, or not
as ordered may be rejected within a reasonable time of delivery, and our
receiving team will tell you which goods are rejected and why. Rejected
goods are held for you to collect or are returned at your cost, as you
prefer, and you will either replace them or credit them, as our buyer
chooses.

Records. Please keep a record of what was shipped against each of our
orders, with the carrier and the date, for at least as long as the law
requires. When our buyer asks about a delivery, we would be grateful for an
answer within two working days, with the carrier's proof of delivery where
there is one. Where a delivery is disputed, the record kept by our receiving
team is what we rely on until the matter is settled.

Safety. Every delivery driver must follow the safety rules at our dock, wear
the protective clothing our site requires and stay in the marked areas. Our
receiving team may refuse to unload a vehicle that is not safe to unload.
Hazardous goods must be shipped with the documents the law requires, and
their safety sheets must be sent to our buyer before the first delivery and
again whenever they change.

Returns. Goods returned to you for any reason will be packed as carefully as
they arrived and sent with a note that names the original order and the
reason for the return. Please arrange collection within ten working days of
our request, or tell us that you would rather we send them back by carrier.
A return does not cancel the rest of the order unless our buyer says so in
writing.

Changes to an order. An order may be changed or cancelled only by our buyer,
in writing. A change made by telephone must be confirmed by email before you
act on it. If you receive two messages that seem to contradict each other,
please ask our buyer which one stands rather than choosing one yourself. A
change does not alter the price of anything already shipped.

Confidentiality. The prices, quantities and delivery details in our orders
are confidential between our two companies. Please do not share them with
anyone outside your business except your carrier, and only as far as the
carrier needs them to make the delivery. Drawings and samples we lend you
remain ours and must be returned when we ask for them.

Contact. Questions about an order go to the buyer who placed it. Questions
about an invoice or a payment go to our accounts team. Questions about a
delivery on the day go to our receiving team. If you are not sure whom to
ask, write to the buyer, who will pass the question on. We read every
message, and we are grateful for your care with our orders.

Lead times. Please tell our buyer, when you confirm an order, how long each
item will take to reach us. If a lead time changes after you have confirmed
it, tell our buyer at once rather than on the day the goods were due. We
plan our own work around the dates you give us, so a date that slips without
warning costs us far more than a date that was honest from the start.

Confirmation. Please confirm each order by email within one working day of
receiving it, naming any item you cannot supply and any date you cannot
meet. An order that is not confirmed in that time will be treated as
accepted as written. A confirmation that changes the order is not an
acceptance; it is a new offer, and nothing changes until our buyer agrees to
it in writing.

Labels and marks. Every item that carries a label must carry the label
agreed with our buyer, in the place agreed, and nothing else. Please do not
add your own price labels or promotional stickers to goods intended for us.
Barcodes, where agreed, must scan cleanly at the first attempt; goods whose
barcodes do not scan will be relabelled by our team and the cost of that
work charged to you.

Storage before shipping. Goods held for us before shipping must be kept dry,
clean and away from direct sunlight, and must not be stacked so high that
the cartons at the bottom are crushed. If you hold goods for us at our
request, tell our buyer how long you are able to hold them and whether a
charge applies, before the holding begins rather than afterwards.

Carriers. Please use the carriers our buyer has agreed with you, or a
carrier of the same standing. Every carrier must give our receiving team a
proof of delivery to sign, and must not leave goods at the dock without a
signature. If a carrier damages goods on the way to us, please deal with the
carrier directly and send us replacements without waiting for the claim to
be settled.

Insurance. Goods remain at your risk until they are signed for at our dock.
Please keep insurance that covers goods in transit and in your care for
their full value. If you are asked to hold goods for us, they remain at your
risk while you hold them, unless our buyer agrees otherwise in writing.

Environment. Please keep packing to what the goods need to arrive safely,
and use packing that can be recycled where you are able to. We return
reusable pallets and crates when the carrier is able to take them, and we
ask that you take back any packing that we cannot recycle locally. If you
have a scheme for returning packing, please tell our buyer about it.

Samples and trials. When our buyer asks for a sample or a trial quantity,
please send it with a note that says so clearly, so that our receiving team
does not book it in as an ordinary delivery. Samples are not orders, and a
sample does not commit us to any later purchase. If a sample is to be
returned, please say so on the note and we will send it back.

Seasonal closures. Our receiving dock is closed on public holidays and for a
short period at the turn of the year. Our buyer will tell you the dates well
in advance. Please do not plan deliveries for those days; a delivery that
arrives while we are closed will be turned away and the cost of the second
attempt will fall on the carrier you chose.

Disputes. If you and our buyer disagree about anything to do with an order,
please write to our buyer first and set out the facts as you see them. Most
matters are settled quickly that way. If a matter cannot be settled between
you and our buyer, either side may ask for it to be passed to a manager on
each side, who will meet or speak within a reasonable time to settle it.

Changes to these terms. We may change these terms from time to time, and we
will always tell you in writing before a change applies. A change does not
affect orders already confirmed unless both of our companies agree that it
should. Where these terms differ from a written agreement signed by both our
companies, the signed agreement wins.

Your own terms. Terms printed on your quotes, confirmations, delivery notes
or invoices do not apply to our orders unless our buyer has agreed to them
in writing. We mention this only so that nobody is surprised; we are happy
to discuss any term that matters to you, and our buyer will gladly take any
question to the right person on our side.

Payment details. If your bank details change, please tell our accounts team
by letter on your company paper, signed by a director, and confirm the
change by telephone to the number we already hold for you. We will never act
on a change of bank details sent by email alone, and we ask you to treat any
such email that seems to come from us with the same caution.

Shortages. If you find that you cannot supply the full quantity of an item,
please ship what you have only if our buyer agrees, and say on the packing
slip how much is still to come. Please never make up a shortage by sending
more of a different item. Our buyer would always rather hear about a
shortage early than find it at the dock.

Over-deliveries. Please send exactly what was ordered. Goods sent beyond the
quantity on the order may be refused at the dock, or held for you to collect
at your cost, and they will not be paid for unless our buyer agrees in
writing to keep them. A small over-delivery made to fill a standard carton
must be agreed with our buyer before the goods are shipped.

Documents with each delivery. Each delivery must come with a delivery note
that matches the packing slips, and, where the goods need them, the
certificates our buyer has asked for. A delivery that arrives without the
documents it needs may be held at the dock, unopened, until the documents
arrive by email or with a later delivery.

Visits. Our buyer may ask to visit your premises, at a time that suits you
both, to see how our goods are made, stored or packed. We will always give
notice and keep to your own site rules. Equally, you are welcome to visit
our receiving dock to see how deliveries are handled, and our receiving team
will be glad to show you around.

Your people. Please make sure that everyone at your company who handles our
orders has seen these terms, including the people who pack and ship the
goods and the people who send the invoices. It is often the smallest detail
on a packing slip or an invoice that decides whether a delivery is booked in
quickly or held for questions.

Notices. Any notice under these terms is given in writing, by email to the
buyer who placed the order or by letter to our registered office. A notice
sent by email counts as received on the working day after it is sent, unless
the sender is told that it did not arrive. Please keep a copy of every
notice you send us, as we will of every notice we send you.

Thank you for your help with all of the above. We know that these terms are
longer than the last ones, and we are grateful to every supplier who reads
them through. If anything here is unclear, or seems to conflict with an
agreement you already have with us, please ask before you ship rather than
after, and our buyer will answer as quickly as possible.

